  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Since \\(M\\) lies in the second quadrant, \\(a<0\\) and \\(b>0\\). The symmetric point \\((-a,-b)\\) has a positive x-coordinate and a negative y-coordinate, so it lies in the fourth quadrant.",
